+# issuer-private-sqlite-cache
+## Requirements
+- `admission`: Both pure plans and all additional interfaces accept host configuration only. If configuration is absent or enabled is not exactly true or resourceAdmission.status is not exactly 'received', return null from plans; withIssuerSqliteStore returns {status:'not-configured'} without calling work or touching storage; private handler returns HTTP404 without storage. Once admitted require cacheKey a nonempty string whose UTF8 length is at most256 bytes, and maximumCohortBytes a positive safe integer no greater than524288; cacheKey must differ from 'registers/earning-loops/issuer-research.json', otherwise throw TypeError before effects. Ignore additional trusted metadata. These guards grant no resource or source authority.
+- `coordinates`: issuerSqliteStoragePlan(configuration) is pure and returns exactly {cohortKey:'issuer-evidence/cohort',statusKey:'issuer-evidence/status',logicalStatusKey:'registers/earning-loops/issuer-research.json',cacheKey:configuration.cacheKey,maximumCohortBytes:configuration.maximumCohortBytes,maximumStatusBytes:524288,maximumTransactionBytes:1900000}. issuerEvidenceReadPlan(configuration) is pure and returns exactly {objectName:'earning-loops',path:'/issuer-evidence',cacheKey:configuration.cacheKey,maximumCohortBytes:configuration.maximumCohortBytes}. These are real transport/storage plans used by additional interfaces; no fixture-mode APIs.
+## Prohibitions
+- `no-authority-expansion`: No public cache or refresh route, source acquisition, OpenTask/credential read, arbitrary key, alarm mutation, new namespace, schedule, external dependency, private worker package import or deployment. [claims: bounded-cache]
+## Laws
+- `byte-custody` | IETF | RFC9110 | https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110 | Private GET and response representation preserve actual body bytes and length; retrieval does not authorize refresh. | Correct status and media semantics, no hidden mutations on GET.
